\lispPackageChapter{sigma}

The \texttt{sigma} package is the umbrella package for the library.  It uses
every subordinate package and re-exports a short list of entry points for
loading the whole system into the current package.

\section{Variables}

\lispVariableSubsection{*sigma-packages*}

The \texttt{*sigma-packages*} variable holds a list of all Sigma package
designators.  \texttt{use-all-sigma} walks this list.  The default value is

\begin{lstlisting}
(:sigma/behave
 :sigma/control
 :sigma/hash
 :sigma/numeric
 :sigma/os
 :sigma/probability
 :sigma/random
 :sigma/sequence
 :sigma/string
 :sigma/time-series
 :sigma/truth
 :sigma)
\end{lstlisting}

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{use-all-sigma}

The \texttt{use-all-sigma} function calls \texttt{use-package} on every package
in \texttt{*sigma-packages*} from the current package, making all of their
external symbols available without package prefixes.  This will pollute
\texttt{common-lisp-user} if that is your current package; that is intentional
for interactive use.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(use-all-sigma)}

\lispExamples

\begin{lstlisting}
(asdf:load-system :sigma)
(sigma:use-all-sigma)
(sum (loop for i from 1 to 100 collect i)) ; Returns 5050
\end{lstlisting}
